# The catalog cannot be read from the launch until the `modelsup` line, and
# the inline column is open over the failure with nothing running. A frame
# reads a failed catalog again only past the failure's hold -- 5 s after the
# first failure in a row, 10 s after the second (`failureBackoffMs`,
# `beginLoad`, `model_cache_runtime.zig:40-54`, `:617@481104fd`) -- and fx
# paints a frame only when something asks for one (`flushRequestedFrame`,
# `app_render_runtime.zig:928-929`): nothing animates while idle, so the
# column's render path -- the only thing that asks the cache again
# (`footerContext`, `:561-563`) -- does not run. The column opens past the
# launch read's 5 s and reads again (503); once it is on the screen over the
# failure, the catalog comes back; `col-idle`,
# past that read's 10 s, still says `unable to load models`, and the next
# keystroke's frame asks again and lists the rows. The outage ends at a line,
# not at a moment on the gateway's clock, which each binary's launch reaches
# at a different time (registry #19). `modelsdelay 0` stamps each read in the
# gateway log.
models models.json
modelsdown
modelsdelay 0
wait 6
type /model
key Space
until shown unable to load models
wait 0.8
snap col-down
modelsup
wait 11
snap col-idle
type o
until shown gpt-6-astra
snap col-typed
gwlog
